      "sourceTextSha256": "337b4fbdb94ee769b975fb8b7311e0d8d4806fd28f146cfd91ac2aa0b465272c",
      "text": "Brazilian side of Iguazú Falls",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-mw6kxp21-vlap279rsy",
        "model": "GPT-6"
      }
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:d1bf136a4a3c936a",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "48927128822a5a57bebd5a880cdcf4672c55ac2a797532287ffc56eecf2f9fb9",
      "text": "After breakfast, head out on a guided tour of the Brazilian side of Iguazú Falls, where you can see the full sweep of the falls. The name comes from Guarani and means “Big Water”. The system consists of 275 individual falls.\n\nTrails and viewpoints along the route look out over the cascades and the Devil's Throat. In places, the walkways come so close to the water that mist hangs in the air. From the Brazilian side, you can take in several cascades at once and see the scale of the whole system.\n\n**Exotic bird park at Iguazú**\n\nYou can add a visit to the Bird Park for $50 per person.\n\n**Helicopter flight over Iguazú Falls**\n\nYou can also take a helicopter flight over the falls for $170 per person.\n\nAfter the tour, transfer to your hotel. The evening is free to relax after your day at the falls.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-mw6kxp21-vlap279rsy",
        "model": "GPT-6"
      }
    },
